{"id": 1632, "result": [{"value": {"choices": []}, "id": "ltlOui2VyY", "from_name": "flags", "to_name": "image", "type": "choices", "origin": "prediction"}, {"value": {"choices": ["No Error"]}, "id": "8pGTVgbJd9", "from_name": "severity", "to_name": "gpt-output", "type": "choices", "origin": "prediction-changed"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.2, "y": 8.3, "width": 71.7, "height": 29.4, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_1", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.2, "y": 8.3, "width": 71.7, "height": 29.4, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "BB_1", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.2, "y": 8.3, "width": 71.7, "height": 29.4, "rotation": 0, "text": ["See that the only difference between a quasi-equilibrium and an equilibrium is given by condition 2. Essentially, if xi is preferred to xi*, it must cost at least as much. If wi = pxi* then xi* minimizes the expenditure px on the contour set V(x*). Note that if instead it said \"xi \u2265i x* i =\u21d2 pxi > wi*\" then this would mean that xi* is optimal in the budget set, since any other bundle that is better, could not be in the budget set."]}, "id": "BB_1", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.6, "y": 42.7, "width": 9.3, "height": 4.5, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_2", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.6, "y": 42.7, "width": 9.3, "height": 4.5, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "BB_2", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.6, "y": 42.7, "width": 9.3, "height": 4.5, "rotation": 0, "text": ["Theorem "]}, "id": "BB_2", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.3, "y": 48.6, "width": 70.5, "height": 17.7, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_3", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.3, "y": 48.6, "width": 70.5, "height": 17.7, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "BB_3", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.3, "y": 48.6, "width": 70.5, "height": 17.7, "rotation": 0, "text": ["Suppose Yi is convex for all j = 1, 2, ..., J and the preference relations \u2265i are rational, convex and satisfy local non-satiation. Then, for any Pareto-Optimal Allocation (x*, y*), there exist a price vector p \u2208 R+ such that (x*, y* , p) is a price quasi-equilibrium with transfers"]}, "id": "BB_3", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.2, "y": 73.8, "width": 70.1, "height": 17.8, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_4", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.2, "y": 73.8, "width": 70.1, "height": 17.8, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "BB_4", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.2, "y": 73.8, "width": 70.1, "height": 17.8, "rotation": 0, "text": ["The idea of the theorem is to generalize the argument of the second welfare theorem for the 1x1 model. We will define an analog of the set V* = {x : x \u2265 x*} and the technology Y*, and find the implementing equilibrium prices by finding the separating hyperplane between both."]}, "id": "BB_4", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 20.795454545454547, "y": 0.6060606060606061, "width": 28.295454545454547, "height": 3.636363636363637, "rotation": 0}, "id": "5SBtZ-vTaA", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "manual"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 20.795454545454547, "y": 0.6060606060606061, "width": 28.295454545454547, "height": 3.636363636363637, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "5SBtZ-vTaA", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "manual"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 20.795454545454547, "y": 0.6060606060606061, "width": 28.295454545454547, "height": 3.636363636363637, "rotation": 0, "text": ["Alternative Proof for the Second Welfare Theorem"]}, "id": "5SBtZ-vTaA", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "manual"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 17.215909090909093, "y": 96.66666666666667, "width": 16.19318181818182, "height": 2.7272727272727195, "rotation": 0}, "id": "iHfNsDAGfo", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "manual"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 17.215909090909093, "y": 96.66666666666667, "width": 16.19318181818182, "height": 2.7272727272727195, "rotation": 0, "labels